{"text":"I can see the issue clearly. The `pageBounds` function in `src/paginate.js` uses an inclusive end offset (`start + pageSize - 1`), but the tests expect an exclusive end offset (like array slicing).\n\nCurrent behavior:\n- `pageBounds(2, 10, 23)` returns `{ start: 20, end: 23 }` — but with inclusive math it would return `{ start: 20, end: 29 }` clamped to 23. Wait, let me re-check: `Math.min(20 + 10 - 1, 23) = Math.min(29, 23) = 23`. So it returns `{ start: 20, end: 23 }`.\n\nTest expects: `{ start: 20, end: 23 }` for page 2, size 10, total 23. That's records 20, 21, 22 (3 records on the partial final page). With exclusive end, that's correct.\n\nSecond test: `pageBounds(0, 10, 10)` expects `{ start: 0, end: 10 }`. Current code: `Math.min(0 + 10 - 1, 10) = Math.min(9, 10) = 9`. So it returns `{ start: 0, end: 9 }`, but the test expects `{ start: 0, end: 10 }`.\n\nThe fix is to change `start + pageSize - 1` to `start + pageSize` (exclusive end):","toolCalls":[{"callId":"call_d15cdff13f2442bf9c7a3df2","name":"filesystem.patch","arguments":{"expectedDigest":"sha256:07e80059ae02fafc7c48d67fc6a0e24538777fb5b8687cfbabd6575970061f70","find":"const end = Math.min(start + pageSize - 1, total);","path":"src/paginate.js","replace":"const end = Math.min(start + pageSize, total);"}}],"finishReason":"tool_calls"}